WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:03.458
Yep.

00:00:05.542 --> 00:00:07.000
-Nope.
-Yep.

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:14.833
You cheater!

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:20.042
Well, that was productive.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.875
Wait! Oh my God,
I just remembered something.

00:00:24.708 --> 00:00:25.708
No!

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:28.167
Wait, is that
what I think it is?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:29.917
Here's our beach
bucket list!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.458
-What?
-Oh my God.

00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:32.583
A long time ago,

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:35.292
Lee and I put together a
list of all the crazy things

00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:37.667
we wanted to do together
before going to college.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.042
It was all of our childhood
summertime dreams

00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:42.250
and fantasies listed out

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.875
on one very important
piece of paper.

00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:47.208
Damn, we put together
a solid list.

00:00:47.292 --> 00:00:48.292
We did.

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:50.125
Good morning!

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.667
It is one o'clock
in the afternoon, sunshine.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.500
Sports drink and aspirin
are to your left.

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:56.625
Oh, yes please.

00:00:56.708 --> 00:00:58.000
One, two, three!

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.583
Go!

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.792
We got a winner!

00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:27.833
We're making
dreams come true!

00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:35.875
Ladies and gentlemen,
we have a winner.

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:37.000
Yeah!

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.625
This is amazing.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:43.083
-You've done this before!
-I swear to you I've not.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:47.917
We built this city
on rock and roll

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.333
We built this city…

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:56.542
We built this city
on rock and roll

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.375
You know, we're not going
to be able to do

00:02:01.458 --> 00:02:03.417
all of
our bucket list items.

00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:06.167
Bucket list item number 22:

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.333
"Live together at Berkeley."

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:11.375
This one was going
to be tricky.

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:13.625
Hey! Erm…

00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:14.667
I've been thinking

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.458
and what if I just went up
with you now?

00:02:17.042 --> 00:02:17.917
We go up to Berkeley.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.125
We'll find an apartment,
get set up.

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:21.667
It'll be like
we're moving in together

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.750
without the actual,
you know, moving in part.

00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:24.958
Hmm…

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.250
I accept your offer.

00:03:22.917 --> 00:03:24.333
I got off the wait list.

00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:26.833
Harvard.

00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:27.875
What?

00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:33.792
Stop, stop! Put me down.

00:03:34.917 --> 00:03:35.875
Shit.

00:03:39.542 --> 00:03:41.417
I can't just not be upset
about this, Elle.

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:44.208
You're leaving me.

00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:49.833
Lee, I don't know
what's going to happen.

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:53.333
But, what I do know is that,
no matter where we are,

00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:56.333
you're always going
to be my best friend.

00:03:56.417 --> 00:03:58.625
Are we still good
for the arcade later?

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.417
Yeah.

00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:03.250
I'm glad you remembered.

00:04:04.042 --> 00:04:06.583
Of course.
I wouldn't miss it.

00:04:07.208 --> 00:04:08.125
Shit!

00:04:16.958 --> 00:04:17.833
Lee?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.167
I'm so sorry.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:22.625
Somehow
I'll make this up to you.

00:04:23.833 --> 00:04:26.375
That is what this
entire summer was about.

00:04:26.958 --> 00:04:28.125
Making it up to me.

00:04:29.458 --> 00:04:30.333
Well, forget it.

00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:31.833
I don't need it.

00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:33.958
You seriously cannot be
this upset.

00:04:34.042 --> 00:04:35.458
It is just a game, Lee.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.042
Is that really what
you think this is about?

00:04:39.958 --> 00:04:41.792
The game?
What, do you think I'm five?

00:04:41.875 --> 00:04:44.083
It's not just about
the damn game, Elle.

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.667
It's about you fighting
for our friendship.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.375
Lee, I know you're upset,
but…

00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:50.208
I don't matter
to you really!

00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:52.083
Not compared to him.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.125
I never have!

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:26.625
I…

00:05:26.708 --> 00:05:28.000
I heard about you and Noah.

00:05:29.042 --> 00:05:29.917
Yeah.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.208
So then come to Berkeley
with me!

00:05:32.292 --> 00:05:33.208
It's worth a shot.

00:05:33.292 --> 00:05:35.333
This is what
I'm talking about, though.

00:05:35.917 --> 00:05:37.792
I chose Boston
to be with Noah

00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:39.375
and Berkeley to be with you.

00:05:41.292 --> 00:05:42.708
I can't figure out who I am…

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:44.917
on my own.

00:05:48.542 --> 00:05:49.417
Come here.

00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:56.375
I'm really sorry about
what I said at the arcade.

00:05:56.875 --> 00:05:58.167
I didn't mean it.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.875
Yeah, I get that.

00:06:02.333 --> 00:06:03.458
That's ok.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:07.833
A lot of it was true.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.875
And I am sorry
we didn't make this

00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:12.875
our most memorable summer
ever.

00:06:13.542 --> 00:06:14.417
I don't know.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.833
That may be exactly
what we did.

00:06:20.208 --> 00:06:21.667
It feels so weird
to be leaving without you.

00:06:27.917 --> 00:06:29.750
I added a new one.

00:06:33.875 --> 00:06:35.125
Rule number 35:

00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:38.417
"Always call your bestie
every time you miss them."

00:06:41.042 --> 00:06:42.167
I love it. Thank you.

00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:15.750
Hey, what's up?

00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:18.583
-I think I got in!
-Yes!

00:07:23.917 --> 00:07:25.792
Ok. You have to tell me more
what happened.

00:07:27.625 --> 00:07:29.625
So, Lee and Rachel
did end up

00:07:29.708 --> 00:07:31.333
getting back together again.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.958
It turns out that,
sometimes,

00:07:33.042 --> 00:07:34.708
people do find their way
back to each other.

00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:38.583
Lee and I stayed connected
all through college

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:39.958
and, after graduation,

00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:41.792
Lee moved back
to Los Angeles.

00:07:41.875 --> 00:07:44.708
And, for us, it was like
no time had passed at all.

00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:46.958
We had both changed a lot,

00:07:47.042 --> 00:07:49.250
but our friendship hadn't.

00:07:49.333 --> 00:07:50.875
And, in the fall
of that year,

00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:54.583
we all found our way back
to a very familiar place.

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:55.667
Oh my God!

00:07:56.625 --> 00:07:58.042
No way!

00:07:58.125 --> 00:08:00.083
And, suddenly, there it was!

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.542
-Lee!
-They're still doing this?

00:08:02.625 --> 00:08:03.875
They're still doing this!

00:08:04.375 --> 00:08:05.542
Oh my God!

